              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for to doubt, then the Persian for to take."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: نجات دادن",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "نجات دادن — nejât dâdan — \"to rescue, to save\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "nejât dâdan pairs nejât, borrowed from Arabic najāt, \"rescue, deliverance\" (root n-j-w, Lane), with the Persian verb dâdan, \"to give\". dâdan, \"to give\", is an inherited verb; EtymDB takes it back to the Indo-European root deh₃-, \"to give\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
